<p align="left" class="body1"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-29 | Wednesday</font></strong><br/><br/>so last night the treacherous three, that is, Geo, RA and myself rocked
the Independent on Divisadero.  big up to Mr. Lif and The Coup for
putting us on.  much love to the bay area fam that hosted us (leonard
shek) and gave us tips on where to eat.  <br>
<br>
golden flower in chinatown for pho.<br>
mama's in the north beach for filthy omelettes.<br>
<br>
and who could forget, the best tapsilog in the south bay not cooked by your auntie!<br>
<br>
<img align="middle" alt="luckychances" height="171" title="luckychances" width="250"><br>
<br>
that's what it do. we're about to hit up san luis obispo today to start the tour with Dan The Automator.  we'll keep ya posted.<br>
<br>
saba<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-28 | Tuesday</font></strong><br/><br/>hearing accounts of snow drifts in the town makes me just a little bit home sick, at least until i step outside to dimaggio park where a large group of seniors are basking in the morning sun, their tai chi postures casting long shadows across the lawn.  <strong>north beach </strong>is certified DOAP.  last night's dinner was the first to top salvatore's in years, and breakfast at <strong>mama's </strong>was the kind travel writers live for.  italian folks make the greatest hosts, and it's becoming abundantly evident to me how sinatra could have left his heart in this community.<br><br>big up's to the hawks for pulling off a miracle of sorts as the elements made it seem like they were visitors at lambeau.  the victory was much needed to lift geo's spirits, dampened by a relentless head-cold.  keep sendin' those positive, healing-type vibes, fam.<br><br>i'm lookin' forward to the reunion with <strong>boots </strong>tonight.  rumor has it the spot is "uber fresh," and speaking from recent experience, aint too much poppin' in downtown frisco on a weeknight.  bring 'em out, bring 'em out...<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-27 | Monday</font></strong><br/><br/>whaddup, fam.  all's well.  we crossed the bay bridge at the stroke of
midnight doin' 80mph with sabz behind the wheel.  an able pilot he is,
but it's geo that deserves capitano props for navigating through a
snow-storm and one hellacious construction-related traffic jam in the
oregonian mountains.  carsickness is kryptonite.<br><br>respect due to
the homie big L for housin' us - i slept well, got a shower and i'm
bouts to get mocha'd up in a minute.  after that i'm trynna find some
new music to cruise to ("i thought you were gonna make the tour
mixtape."  no i thought YOU were gonna make the tour mixtape..."), then
take in the sights and sounds of the bay; seein' sunshine on the
rooftops and hearin' kids kick it at recess has made for a beautiful
first impression.<br><br>more later.  i need a cup of frisco's finest.<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-24 | Friday</font></strong><br/><br/>award tour.<br><br>the whole MassLine fam heads down to PDX today to rock the doug fir for all our northern oregonian brethrenian.  after that we'll take a tour of the alternative lifestyles of eugene and share with the locals some of the sounds of seattle.<br><br>in the bay, Blue Scholars open for Mr. Lif (big up for checkin out the showbox on wednesday, Liffy!) and The Coup <br>at The Independent and then Common Market heads south to hop on Dan The Automator's tour.<br><br>check in with us for the next couple weeks as we will be (attempting to) update you on a daily basis about the westkoast adventures.  maybe we'll even get some pictures.<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-11-22 | Wednesday</font></strong><br/><br/>Doors are at 8pm. See you there.<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><center><div class="pagenumbers"><a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-b6f35646d585.php">[&lt;&lt;]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-ff41e4b899bf.php">[1]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-f09e4ab70de0.php">[2]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-13fd6b501db4.php">[3]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a6d8d32ad781.php">[4]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-d45f54b0cbc4.php">[5]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-0bfc403792bc.php">[6]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-fd78b8847920.php">[7]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-cd30dd4ecbb4.php">[8]</a> <a href="/bl